v0.5.2: fifth-fish
 - [BugFix] NAs.Cast to the string type filled the data with nil pointers, the same convention violation v0.5.1 fixed in Append, one call further down; a mixed list such as ['a', na] in downstream preludio crashed on it. An audit found no further nil builders in the series package

v0.5.1: frank-was-just-asking
 - [BugFix] Strings.Append(NAs) filled the appended data with nil pointers instead of the interned NA text; the first operator to read them crashed (found through preludio, where ['a', na] + 'f' took down the VM)
 - [Feature] meta gains the week duration term and symbols (TERM_DURATION_WEEK, weeks/w); the vocabulary jumped from day to month and a downstream week literal compiled to no instruction

v0.5.0: the-others
 - [Changed] The one-implementation DataFrame interface is collapsed into the concrete type: NewDataFrame, NewDataFrameFromArrowRecord
 - [Changed] Error accessors are the standard Err() error on Series and DataFrame (replacing IsError/GetError/IsErrored)
 - [Changed] Accessor renames: Context, Partition, NullMask, ColIndex (the Get prefix is dropped); IsSorted is SortOrder; the column accessors are Col, ColAt, NameAt, ColIndex (replacing C and At); the join constants are JoinInner/JoinLeft/JoinRight/JoinOuter on JoinType
 - [Changed] The variadic Take is replaced by Slice(start, end) and TakeIndices(indices) on Series and DataFrame
 - [Changed] Reading starts from package-level constructors (dataframe.ReadCsv(ctx), ReadParquet, ...); writers are WriteCsv, WriteParquet, ...; the builder types are exported
 - [Changed] Select matches exact names only; pattern selection moved to SelectMatching (unanchored regular expressions)
 - [Changed] The internal series fields (Data_, NullMask_, ...) are unexported. Data() and the typed accessors (Float64s(), Bools(), ...) are documented views of the backing storage; Strings gains Interned(), every type gains PackedNullMask(); FilterIntSlice and the sort internals (Less, Equal, Swap) leave the Series interface; TakeIndices is the validated path
 - [Changed] NA propagation holds for every binary operator and both operand orders: String + NA and Bool OR NA yield NA (no more NA-text concatenation or value copying), and x - NA is NA instead of an error. Coalesce is the documented exception
 - [Changed] Join output row order is part of the contract: rows follow the left frame's row order, a right join follows the right frame, and an outer join puts the unmatched right rows last. The order was nondeterministic before (#24)
 - [Feature] Coalesce on every series type: fill null elements from another series or a scalar; a result element is null only when both operands are null there
 - [Feature] Not is callable through the Series interface on every type
 - [Feature] SAS7BDAT reading via kshedden/datareader (read-only; use XPT to hand data to SAS)
 - [Removed] The SeriesNumeric interface: nothing implemented or used it
 - [BugFix] SelectAt kept only out-of-bounds indices (inverted bounds check) and always failed
 - [Improved] The generated operator code is flattened from ~44k to ~13k lines with byte-identical behavior; the generator output is gofmt-canonical and stable under a single go generate
 - [Improved] The legacy double-underscore helper names are retired
 - [Improved] grpc, thrift and x/net raised past known vulnerabilities
 - [Improved] New tests: the join contract, Slice/TakeIndices/SelectAt, a CSV write/read round trip, the data-view contracts, NA propagation across operators

v0.4.2: fifth-and-sixth-fish
 - [BugFix] CSV writer: overwriting an existing file truncates it first, in every writer path, so a shorter write no longer leaves the old tail behind (#22, thanks @sjh9714)
 - [BugFix] CSV writer: write errors are reported instead of silently ignored

v0.4.1: not-much
 - [BugFix] meta.SYMBOL_BINARY_AND was "not" instead of "and"
 - [Improved] Select documents that its patterns are unanchored regular expressions

v0.4.0: what-s-new
 - [Feature] Single-pass, parallel hash aggregation behind GroupBy().Agg(): the Q1 sum-by-id benchmark (1e7 rows) goes from ~142ms to ~31ms
 - [Feature] Any/All bool aggregators (Bools result, skip-null default)
 - [Changed] Agg results are sorted by group key (ascending, nulls last); nulls are skipped by default and RemoveNAs(false) makes an NA in a group turn that group's result NA
 - [Changed] GroupBy is lazy: partitions are built on demand
 - [Changed] Terminology: "NaN-poisoning" is now "NA propagation" in the docs and internals

v0.3.0: fourth-fish
 - [Changed] Arrow interop uses arrow.RecordBatch (DataFrame.ToArrowRecord and NewBaseDataFrameFromArrowRecord); arrow.Record was deprecated upstream
 - [BugFix] Aggregations: grouped std used the average group size as divisor; ungrouped mean/std under removeNAs divided by the total length instead of the non-null count
 - [Changed] Evaluated Arrow-native column storage (three-regime benchmark) and decided against it; Arrow stays an interop layer (Parquet, IPC, ecosystem handoff). See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-08-arrow-native-storage-migration.md
 - [Removed] Measurement-only Arrow-native storage prototype and the unwired Arrow compute-dispatch layer (series/arrow_ops.go); neither was reachable outside its own tests. Arrow interop (Series.ArrowArray / ArrowArrayToSeries) is unchanged

v0.2.0: third-fish
 - [Changed] Library renamed from aargh to enchanter: module is now github.com/caerbannogwhite/enchanter, root package is `enchanter`
 - [Feature] Apache Arrow interop: Series.ArrowArray(), DataFrame.ArrowSchema() / ToArrowRecord(), NewBaseDataFrameFromArrowRecord()
 - [Feature] Parquet reader and writer: DataFrame.FromParquet() / ToParquet()
 - [Feature] Arrow IPC (Feather) reader and writer: DataFrame.FromArrowIPC() / ToArrowIPC()
 - [Improved] Aggregators improved, dataframe integration tests added
 - [Improved] Arrow memory: internal Arrow references are released deterministically (CheckedAllocator-clean)
 - [BugFix] Join: fixed right-dataframe column lookup
 - [BugFix] GroupBy: null group keys stay null in the result; grouping by Time/Duration keys no longer corrupts the frame; GroupBy on a grouped dataframe now regroups instead of being ignored
 - [BugFix] Parquet / Arrow IPC readers: null masks are preserved across multiple row groups / record batches
 - [BugFix] Series mutated after an Arrow conversion (Sort, Set) no longer serve stale Arrow data
 - [BugFix] Library code no longer prints debug output to stdout (constructor warnings go to stderr)
 - [Improved] Added examples
 - [WIP] SAS7BDAT reader: header and page parsing only; data reading deferred to a future release

v0.1.2: second-fish
